# quinine.msf
# Quinine  pKa1=4.130 (quinolinium N3→neutral, q=+2→+1)
#          pKa2=8.520 (quinuclidine N→neutral, q=+1→0)
# Source: Perrin 1981 / NIST
# Antimalarial. Two distinct N-bases: quinolinium (aromatic, pKa=4.13)
# and quinuclidinium (aliphatic bicyclic, pKa=8.52). The quinolinium step
# tests the model on a protonated heteroaromatic N with an OMe substituent.
# The quinuclidinium step is the most geometrically constrained bicyclic amine
# in the test set — compare with quinuclidine training compound (pKa=10.95);
# quinine has lower pKa because the adjacent aromatic ring withdraws electrons.
# Historically important: quinine pKa defined the Henderson-Hasselbalch
# framework for antimalarial accumulation in the acidic parasite food vacuole.

